ps5-btusb-iw620-quirks.patch: make the PS5 IW620 Bluetooth quirks take effect on 7.3

Apply after rmuxnet/ps5-linux-patches-1 linux.patch (36f173f).

The IW620 (USB 1286:2059) reports the Bluetooth class in its device
descriptor, so the generic USB_DEVICE_INFO(0xe0, 0x01, 0x01) entry at the
top of btusb_table matches it first, with driver_info 0. The 7.3 port only
lists the device in btusb_table, after the generic entries, and checks the
interface-number flags before the quirks_table lookup, so none of the IW620
flags apply.

As in ps5-linux-patches #35, list the device in quirks_table too and defer
both interface-number checks until after that lookup.

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
index 21baba3..ca1b5fc 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -498,6 +498,17 @@ static const struct usb_device_id quirks_table[] = {
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x1286, 0x2044), .driver_info = BTUSB_MARVELL },
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x1286, 0x2046), .driver_info = BTUSB_MARVELL },
 	{ USB_DEVICE(0x1286, 0x204e), .driver_info = BTUSB_MARVELL },
+
+	/*
+	 * PS5 IW620. The device descriptor carries the Bluetooth class, so
+	 * the generic entry in btusb_table matches first and the flags only
+	 * take effect from here.
+	 */
+	{ USB_DEVICE(0x1286, 0x2059), .driver_info = BTUSB_MARVELL |
+						     BTUSB_IFNUM_0 |
+						     BTUSB_BROKEN_LE_DEFAULT_PHY |
+						     BTUSB_BROKEN_READ_LOCAL_NAME |
+						     BTUSB_NO_AUTOSUSPEND },
 
 	/*
 	 * NXP IW610 BT interfaces (Marvell-lineage silicon, same quirk as
@@ -4208,15 +4219,6 @@ static int btusb_probe(struct usb_interface *intf,
 
 	BT_DBG("intf %p id %p", intf, id);
 
-	if ((id->driver_info & BTUSB_IFNUM_2) &&
-	    (intf->cur_altsetting->desc.bInterfaceNumber != 0) &&
-	    (intf->cur_altsetting->desc.bInterfaceNumber != 2))
-		return -ENODEV;
-
-	if ((id->driver_info & BTUSB_IFNUM_0) &&
-		intf->cur_altsetting->desc.bInterfaceNumber != 0)
-		return -ENODEV;
-
 	ifnum_base = intf->cur_altsetting->desc.bInterfaceNumber;
 
 	if (!id->driver_info) {
@@ -4228,6 +4230,19 @@ static int btusb_probe(struct usb_interface *intf,
 			id = match;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Check these after quirks_table: class-matched devices arrive here
+	 * with driver_info 0 and acquire their interface restriction above.
+	 */
+	if ((id->driver_info & BTUSB_IFNUM_2) &&
+	    (intf->cur_altsetting->desc.bInterfaceNumber != 0) &&
+	    (intf->cur_altsetting->desc.bInterfaceNumber != 2))
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	if ((id->driver_info & BTUSB_IFNUM_0) &&
+	    intf->cur_altsetting->desc.bInterfaceNumber != 0)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	if (id->driver_info & BTUSB_IGNORE)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
